12
00:59:27,272 --> 00:59:33,272
Nanny McPhee and the Big Bang (released in the United States and Canada as Nanny McPhee Returns) is a 2010 period fantasy comedy film directed by Susanna White, produced by Tim
Bevan, Eric Fellner and Lindsay Doran with music by James Newton Howard and co-produced by StudioCanal, Relativity Media, Working Title Films and Three Strange Angels.

13
01:04:24,545 --> 01:04:30,545
It is a sequel to the 2005 film Nanny McPhee.

14
01:09:21,818 --> 01:09:27,818
It was written by Emma Thompson, based on
Christianna Brand's Nurse Matilda books.

15
01:14:19,090 --> 01:14:25,090
Thompson reprises her role as Nanny McPhee, and it also stars Maggie Gyllenhaal, Ralph
Fiennes, Rhys Ifans, Ewan McGregor, Asa Butterfield and Maggie Smith.

16
01:19:16,363 --> 01:19:22,363
It was theatrically released on 2 April 2010 in Europe by Universal Pictures.

17
01:24:13,636 --> 01:24:19,636
It received positive reviews from critics and it earned
$93.2 million on a $35 million budget.

18
01:29:10,909 --> 01:29:16,909
It also received a Young Artist Award nomination for
Best Performance in a Feature Film.

19
01:34:08,181 --> 01:34:14,181
The film was released on DVD and Blu-ray in the UK on 19 June 2010.

20
01:39:05,454 --> 01:39:11,454
The film explores themes of nanny, nostalgic,
aftercreditsstinger, duringcreditsstinger, woman director.

